    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.clue\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen a key binding has a description, custom clues defined in `config.clues` are ignored. For example, the key combo bound to `MiniSplitjoin.toggle()` will always have its default description \"Toggle arguments\" no matter what I set the custom clue to. \r\n\r\nWould it be good to allow overriding of default descriptions?",
